<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">THE PERSON BEHIND THE SYSTEMS</span><h1>Curiosity, rigor,<br/><span style="color:var(--mint)">and a bias for useful work.</span></h1><p>I work across data science, applied research, and engineering—because solving a difficult problem often means moving fluently between all three.</p></div></section>
<div class="container bio-grid"><div><h2>My approach</h2><p>I'm interested in the entire arc of an applied machine learning problem: understanding what matters, working carefully with data, choosing defensible methods, and building something that remains useful when it leaves a notebook.</p><p>My work has included forecasting, operational intelligence, applied AI interfaces, and multimodal research. These areas look different on the surface, but they share questions I return to repeatedly: what can the data really support, how do we know the system works, and how will people use it?</p><p>I value clear communication as much as technical depth. In practice, the most important contribution is often deciding what not to model, what to measure, and how to make the limitations visible.</p><a href="/work/" class="btn btn-primary">Explore my work ↗</a></div><div><h2>Areas of focus</h2><div class="skill-list"><span>Time Series &amp; Forecasting</span><span>Applied ML</span><span>Experiment Design</span><span>Validation &amp; Metrics</span><span>Python &amp; SQL</span><span>Data Pipelines</span><span>BigQuery</span><span>Cloud Deployment</span><span>Analytics Products</span><span>Language AI</span><span>Multimodal Learning</span></div><hr class="thin-rule"/><h2>Beyond the portfolio</h2><p>I also enjoy turning complex ideas into clear technical writing. My earlier notebook-based blog is still available, and I'm gradually curating it alongside newer applied work.</p><a class="ghost-link" href="/writing/">Browse my writing ↗</a></div></div>
